{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340666",
      "title": "Server vs Client Components",
      "lectureOrder": 146,
      "videoOrder": 136,
      "sourceHash": "096cd5faef1c4042ad85f5dc3dc4a0e5bbdd8d87c8e11bf15e34ca1dce581c38",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.81,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "In the last lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 7.89,
          "en": "we again saw a client component in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.89,
          "end": 12.27,
          "en": "and we did already explore server and client components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.27,
          "end": 17.27,
          "en": "earlier in this course in the essentials course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.43,
          "end": 20.01,
          "en": "But it is important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.01,
          "end": 22.35,
          "en": "these different component types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.35,
          "end": 26.823,
          "en": "why they exist, how they work, and when to use which.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.66,
          "end": 31.14,
          "en": "Because in NextJS applications we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.14,
          "end": 34.74,
          "en": "React Server Components which are components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.74,
          "end": 38.16,
          "en": "that are only rendered on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.16,
          "end": 41.22,
          "en": "So where the entire component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 46.22,
          "en": "is only executed on the server, never on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 49.92,
          "en": "We have these kinds of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.92,
          "end": 54.27,
          "en": "and then we have client components which are also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 54.27,
          "end": 59.27,
          "en": "initially pre-rendered on the server despite their name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 63.78,
          "en": "but which then also can be executed on the client side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 67.42,
          "en": "so in the browser, unlike Server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 68.85,
          "end": 71.37,
          "en": "and the error JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 71.37,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "the component defined in there must be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 76.44,
          "en": "a client component for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 76.44,
          "end": 78.33,
          "en": "And that's simply the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.33,
          "end": 81.36,
          "en": "because in a NextJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.36,
          "end": 86.36,
          "en": "errors cannot just be caused due to problems on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 86.64,
          "end": 91.41,
          "en": "but also potentially because some client side code fails",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 91.41,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "and therefore this error fallback component must be callable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 96.39,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 101.07,
          "en": "That's why we have a client component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 101.07,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "But all the other components we have in this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 107.52000000000001,
          "en": "thus far, all the other page components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 107.52000000000001,
          "end": 110.88,
          "en": "and also our own non-page components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 110.88,
          "end": 114.33,
          "en": "all these components are server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 114.33,
          "end": 119.253,
          "en": "They're only rendered on the server, never on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 120.15,
          "end": 124.74,
          "en": "And you can see that if you console log something in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 124.74,
          "end": 126.483,
          "en": "for example, news list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 131.07,
          "en": "If you do that, you'll notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 131.07,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "that if you open your browser developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 136.68,
          "en": "and they are the JavaScript console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.68,
          "end": 138.6,
          "en": "you won't see any log in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.6,
          "end": 141.15,
          "en": "no matter how much I navigate around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 141.15,
          "end": 143.1,
          "en": "So even though we're in that single page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.1,
          "end": 148.1,
          "en": "application mode here, we don't see any news list log here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.89,
          "end": 151.59,
          "en": "On the other hand, if I opened a terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 151.59,
          "end": 154.29,
          "en": "where the development server is running,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 154.29,
          "end": 158.88,
          "en": "if I reload this news page for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 158.88,
          "end": 161.22,
          "en": "I can see this news list log here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 164.34,
          "en": "which proves that it was executed on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 167.88,
          "en": "because any logs we're seeing here in that terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "where the development server are running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 175.43,
          "en": "are server side logs logs, so produced by server side code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 176.31,
          "end": 181.31,
          "en": "Now by default in NextJS you should keep all your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 184.29,
          "en": "as server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 184.29,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "You should not change them to client components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "if you don't have to because there's just no reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 195.57,
          "en": "to unnecessarily potentially execute some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195.57,
          "end": 198.75,
          "en": "on the client if it's not required to load there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 203.34,
          "en": "Rendering everything on the server is the better strategy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 203.34,
          "end": 206.49,
          "en": "But sometimes you need a client component, for example here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 206.49,
          "end": 208.11,
          "en": "for the error page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 208.11,
          "end": 212.55,
          "en": "but also for another adjustment I wanna make here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 212.55,
          "end": 214.5,
          "en": "that other adjustment I wanna make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 214.5,
          "end": 216.42000000000002,
          "en": "is here in my main header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 216.42000000000002,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "There, I wanna add a second link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 222.36,
          "en": "which leads us to the archive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 222.36,
          "end": 226.47,
          "en": "And for that alone, we don't need a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 226.47,
          "end": 228.24,
          "en": "We can just make it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 228.24,
          "end": 231.993,
          "en": "and keep the main header as a server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.1,
          "end": 235.82999999999998,
          "en": "And with that we now have that archive link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 235.82999999999998,
          "end": 240.24,
          "en": "But now I wanna highlight the currently active link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 240.24,
          "end": 241.92,
          "en": "so not just when we hover over it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 241.92,
          "end": 245.073,
          "en": "but instead when the related page is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 246,
          "end": 248.28,
          "en": "And to do that I need to find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.28,
          "end": 251.52,
          "en": "what the currently active path is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 251.52,
          "end": 255.3,
          "en": "and we can get that currently active path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 255.3,
          "end": 258.54,
          "en": "by using the use path name hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258.54,
          "end": 262.293,
          "en": "which can be imported from next slash navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 263.7,
          "end": 267.39,
          "en": "This gives us a path value, which will be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 267.39,
          "end": 270.753,
          "en": "which is simply the currently active URL path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 271.8,
          "end": 274.40999999999997,
          "en": "We can then use that to find out which link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 274.40999999999997,
          "end": 276.63,
          "en": "should be marked as active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 276.63,
          "end": 279.93,
          "en": "So we can do that by adding a class name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 279.93,
          "end": 284.71,
          "en": "and checking if the path which we got from use path name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 285.65999999999997,
          "end": 290.58299999999997,
          "en": "is equal to slash news in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 291.72,
          "end": 296.72,
          "en": "or let's say whether it starts with slash news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 296.94,
          "end": 301.94,
          "en": "so that nested pops also mark this link as active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 303,
          "end": 304.08,
          "en": "And if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 304.08,
          "end": 307.71,
          "en": "I wanna add a CSS class called active to this link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 307.71,
          "end": 311.22,
          "en": "Otherwise, I'll add undefined as a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 311.22,
          "end": 312.933,
          "en": "so no class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 314.55,
          "end": 317.94,
          "en": "And then we can repeat that on the second link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 317.94,
          "end": 322.053,
          "en": "and just check whether the path starts with slash archive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 323.07,
          "end": 325.02,
          "en": "So with that we have the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 325.02,
          "end": 327.9,
          "en": "for potentially highlighting the links,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 327.9,
          "end": 331.59,
          "en": "but we now would get an error if we save that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 331.59,
          "end": 334.71,
          "en": "We get an error because use path name only works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 334.71,
          "end": 338.61,
          "en": "in client components and we also get the solution here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 338.61,
          "end": 341.15999999999997,
          "en": "that we should add the use client directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 341.15999999999997,
          "end": 342.573,
          "en": "at the top of the file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 343.77,
          "end": 346.65,
          "en": "Well therefore here, we actually now have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 346.65,
          "end": 351.06,
          "en": "to convert this component here to a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 351.06,
          "end": 353.493,
          "en": "because otherwise it won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 354.57,
          "end": 359.57,
          "en": "Because this hook here like most needs a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 359.58,
          "end": 362.103,
          "en": "around it in order to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 362.94,
          "end": 366.39,
          "en": "So therefore here we should add this use client directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 366.39,
          "end": 369.45,
          "en": "at the top of the main header JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 369.45,
          "end": 372.57,
          "en": "and with that added, if you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 372.57,
          "end": 377.25,
          "en": "the error goes away and the active path is highlighted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 377.25,
          "end": 378.843,
          "en": "and stays highlighted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 379.89,
          "end": 383.67,
          "en": "However, this solution has a small flaw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 383.67,
          "end": 385.47,
          "en": "because whilst it works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 385.47,
          "end": 389.94,
          "en": "we now actually also converted a lot of markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 389.94,
          "end": 392.64,
          "en": "to client component markup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 392.64,
          "end": 395.61,
          "en": "even though it wouldn't need to be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 395.61,
          "end": 398.34000000000003,
          "en": "Because we really only need use client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 398.34000000000003,
          "end": 400.23,
          "en": "because of use path name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 400.23,
          "end": 402.48,
          "en": "And we only need that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 402.48,
          "end": 406.02,
          "en": "because of the link component where we wanna add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 406.02,
          "end": 408.363,
          "en": "a CSS class conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 409.47,
          "end": 412.05,
          "en": "And therefore in such scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 412.05,
          "end": 415.83,
          "en": "and in general when working with NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 415.83,
          "end": 420.3,
          "en": "it is considered a good practice to outsource",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 420.3,
          "end": 422.4,
          "en": "that client site code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 422.4,
          "end": 426.48,
          "en": "or that code that requires a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 426.48,
          "end": 431.48,
          "en": "so that your client components are as small as possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 431.76,
          "end": 434.22,
          "en": "so that most of your component logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 434.22,
          "end": 438.423,
          "en": "and markup stays in the server component realm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 439.65,
          "end": 442.08,
          "en": "Hence here I'll add a new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 442.08,
          "end": 446.31,
          "en": "the nav link JS file will hold it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 446.31,
          "end": 450.963,
          "en": "where I'll export my component function nav link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 452.04,
          "end": 456.06,
          "en": "And this component now has the job of outputting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 456.06,
          "end": 459.483,
          "en": "that potentially highlighted navigation link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 460.47,
          "end": 464.43,
          "en": "So I'll actually cut this link component logic here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 464.43,
          "end": 466.86,
          "en": "from the main header JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 466.86,
          "end": 471.633,
          "en": "and add it here as a returned JSX code in nav link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 472.74,
          "end": 477.03,
          "en": "And of course, we now also must copy this link component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
